# Open Ends tracker (Flaux HQ)

This repo has an Open Ends tracker at `OPEN_ENDS.md` tracked by Flaux HQ.

## When you fix something
- If the fix resolves an item listed in `OPEN_ENDS.md`, tick it (`- [x]`) in the **same change** as the fix (same commit when committing).
- Or include `closes OE: <item text>` in the commit message.

## When you notice something new
- If you notice a new bug, SEO gap, missing client input, unbuilt feature, content issue, performance/a11y gap, or launch/infra gap while working, add it under the right section as `- [ ] text #priority`.
- Use `#high` for launch blockers, broken functionality, or indexing harm; otherwise `#medium` or `#low`.
- Do not fix unrelated open ends without asking.

## Never
- Never rename or remove the section headings in `OPEN_ENDS.md` (`## Bugs`, `## SEO`, `## Client inputs needed`, `## Features to build`, `## Content`, `## Performance & accessibility`, `## Launch & infra`).
- Never put secrets, passwords, or API keys in the tracker.
